Language agents combine reasoning, browser actions, and tools ( Nakano et al., 2021 ; Yao et al., 2023b ; Shinn et al., 2023 ; Schick et al., 2023 ; Qin et al., 2024 ) ;
search methods add deliberation or tree expansion at inference time ( Wei et al., 2022 ; Yao et al., 2023a ; Zhou et al., 2024a ; Snell et al., 2025 ; Song et al., 2024 ) ;
and modern web, software, desktop, and embodied benchmarks stress
realistic interfaces ( Zhou et al., 2024b ; Koh et al., 2024 ; Deng et al., 2023 ; Yao et al., 2022 ; Shridhar et al., 2021 ; Yang et al., 2024 ; Xie et al., 2024 ) .
CLIFT differs from prompt-level search because its selector reuses a
certified per-URL bank learned during RL training, not just more samples.
